From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:37:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mali-r32p1: find the context's task without a pid-namespace
 lookup

kbase_context_common_init() records current->tgid - the global id - in
kctx->tgid, then looks the task up again with find_get_pid(kctx->tgid).
find_get_pid() resolves a number in the caller's own pid namespace, not the
global one. So for any process inside a container with a pid namespace of
its own the lookup fails, and creating a GPU context returns -ESRCH:

  mali 13000000.mali: Failed to get pid pointer for surfaceflinger/12594
  mali 13000000.mali: Common context initialization failed error = -3

(or, worse, finds an unrelated task that happens to have that number
inside the namespace). On LuneOS this is Waydroid: Android runs in an LXC
container, its EGL cannot initialise ("Failed creating base context during
initializing of kernel context flags"), SurfaceFlinger aborts with "no
suitable EGLConfig found" every five seconds, and Android never finishes
booting. Processes outside a namespace - the LuneOS compositor - were never
affected.

The task wanted is the caller's thread group leader, which is what the pid
lookup on the tgid returned. Take current->group_leader directly: the same
task, no lookup, no namespace. kctx->tgid itself is left alone; everywhere
else it is only compared against other global ids or logged.

Tested on a Zinwa Q25 (MT6789, Mali-G57): Android in Waydroid reaches
sys.boot_completed with SurfaceFlinger up, and the module's interface is
unchanged - all 386 imported and 132 exported symbol CRCs match the stock
mali_kbase_mt6789.ko.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c  | 46 ++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/mediatek/gpu_mali/mali_valhall/mali-r32p1/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c b/drivers/gpu/mediatek/gpu_mali/mali_valhall/mali-r32p1/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c
index 4f299e5507da..e1df16259636 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/mediatek/gpu_mali/mali_valhall/mali-r32p1/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/mediatek/gpu_mali/mali_valhall/mali-r32p1/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/context/mali_kbase_context.c
@@ -145,37 +145,21 @@ int kbase_context_common_init(struct kbase_context *kctx)
 
 	/* Check if this is a Userspace created context */
 	if (likely(kctx->filp)) {
-		struct pid *pid_struct;
-
-		rcu_read_lock();
-		pid_struct = find_get_pid(kctx->tgid);
-		if (likely(pid_struct)) {
-			struct task_struct *task = pid_task(pid_struct, PIDTYPE_PID);
-
-			if (likely(task)) {
-				/* Take a reference on the task to avoid slow lookup
-				 * later on from the page allocation loop.
-				 */
-				get_task_struct(task);
-				kctx->task = task;
-			} else {
-				dev_err(kctx->kbdev->dev,
-					"Failed to get task pointer for %s/%d",
-					current->comm, current->pid);
-				err = -ESRCH;
-			}
-
-			put_pid(pid_struct);
-		} else {
-			dev_err(kctx->kbdev->dev,
-				"Failed to get pid pointer for %s/%d",
-				current->comm, current->pid);
-			err = -ESRCH;
-		}
-		rcu_read_unlock();
-
-		if (unlikely(err))
-			return err;
+		/* Take a reference on the task to avoid slow lookup later on
+		 * from the page allocation loop.
+		 *
+		 * The task wanted is the caller's thread group leader. It used
+		 * to be found with find_get_pid(kctx->tgid), but kctx->tgid is
+		 * the global id while find_get_pid() resolves a number in the
+		 * caller's own pid namespace - so from any process in a
+		 * container with a pid namespace of its own the lookup failed
+		 * with -ESRCH ("Failed to get pid pointer"), or found an
+		 * unrelated task that happened to have that number there. No
+		 * GPU context could be created in a container at all.
+		 * group_leader is the same task, reached without a lookup.
+		 */
+		get_task_struct(current->group_leader);
+		kctx->task = current->group_leader;
 	}
 
 	/* Check if this is a Userspace created context */
-- 
2.53.0

